From: jamesdborin <james.dborin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:54:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MoE: MOE_FAST_COMBINE fused top-k combine without the f32
 [T,topk,H] intermediate

When the SparseCore dense_gather_reduce kernel is not usable (v6e, topk=6),
the JAX fallback gathers gmm2_res[revert] (bf16 [T*topk, H]), relays it out to
a sublane-padded f32 [T, topk->8, H] and multiply-reduces it (~1.87 ms/layer
at 4096 tokens/chip, 32% of the DSV4-Flash TP8 prefill step).

MOE_FAST_COMBINE=1: XLA, one gather + f32 multiply-add per k; the f32
  relayout disappears (deviceless v6e AOT temp 704 -> 193 MiB, XLA
  bytes-accessed 2981 -> 2159 MiB per layer).
MOE_FAST_COMBINE=2: TensorCore Pallas kernel: per 64-token tile DMA the
  6*64 source rows HBM->VMEM (double-buffered across grid steps; bf16 is
  fetched as uint32 row pairs since 1-row bf16 VMEM slices are not tile
  aligned), f32 weighted accumulate, one write. No HBM temporaries; falls
  back to mode 1 for shapes it does not take.

Both apply to the default (bf16) combine and the MOE_F32_REDUCE combine.
Same math (f32 products, f32 sum over topk, one rounding); the topk sum is
added k = 0..topk-1 (XLA's reduce order may differ on TPU). Default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQhK9cavqLsEnxm6YHREB3
